93f","description":"Perform on Video","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7b58-8066-0684f822118f","description":"Play on Vine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-76f7-867d-24ac3702137f","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes Michelangelo?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Michelangelo was a Renaissance sculptor, painter and architect who also designed the dome of St. Peter\u2019s Basilica; it was completed after his death.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7458-8621-3c71e15dae8a","description":"Renaissance sculptor, painter and architect","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7a47-a247-40a61c5f8d46","description":"Founder of Manichaeism, a gnostic religion which for a time was a rival to Christianity.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-74a5-b505-50e6d8f8a4e7","description":"Inventor and businessman who helped introduce electricity and electric light bulbs.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-768a-b1a4-ce2c0dd0b725","description":"Industrialist who revolutionised mass-production techniques","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7558-a576-540431ccad64","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the marketing slogan of Audi?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Audi\'s German tagline is \u201cVorsprung durch Technik,\u201d commonly rendered in English as \u201cAdvancement Through Technology.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7b77-862e-35c65afddb66","description":"Advancement Through Technology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7411-8470-6884b211723e","description":"Grace, Space, Pace.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7b77-831f-02a2cf02c1d9","description":"There is no substitute","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7e12-8250-24e6b192295e","description":"Think Small","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7375-87b5-88a1769f79b1","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes Asoka?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Asoka was a Mauryan ruler whose rock and pillar edicts promoted moral conduct and tolerance after the Kalinga war.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad64-701b-9bcf-3085561e7509","description":"Powerful Indian King who established a large empire by conquest before converting to Buddhism.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-78ce-90f7-85ba202ab6e4","description":"Queen of England from 1558 to her death in 1603. Cemented England as a Protestant country, defeated Spanish Armada.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7d4a-96f7-d0a53ce048d4","description":"Explorer, first European to reach India and establish a route for imperialism.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-77c7-8fcd-f3940fb4b846","description":"Spiritual Teacher and founder of Buddhism.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7401-9d25-6de5b2ec3497","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What did \'my true love give to me\' on the ninth day of Christmas?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The ninth gift is 9 Ladies Dancing, placed after eight maids a-milking and before ten lords a-leaping in the cumulative song.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad64-72a9-a73b-2a9dfa33306c","description":"9 Ladies Dancing","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7129-b5e9-7435c21b4306","description":"9 Lords a Leaping","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7b3e-baf7-be2e60b6f3f9","description":"9 Calling Birds","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-72cb-9d6e-8598718dc55f","description":"9 Pipers Piping","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad64-7866-81ed-00968c48de19","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What title does the head of government hold in countries with a Westminster system?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A prime minister usually leads the Cabinet and is accountable to the legislature; a monarch, where one exists, is typically head of state.","a